{
  "identification": "ltidisafe npm packages 3.9.9, 4.0.2, 4.0.4; NetworkSpeedCheck module plus install sidecar",
  "evidence": [
    "All original SHA-256 values verified. Each archive contains only index.js, test.js, and package.json. Shared index.js bytes are identical.",
    "preinstall runs node test.js > /dev/null 2>&1; test.js imports the speed-check module and invokes its helper three times at module load.",
    "os.hostname(), os.homedir(), and os.userInfo().username each pass through Buffer.from(value, utf8).toString(hex). The resulting value is the first DNS label of an HTTP URL with an Oastify callback suffix.",
    "The speed-check method selects http or https using URL.protocol, then protocol.get(baseUrl, callback). Data leaves in DNS resolution and the HTTP host. Successful response or speed computation is not required for attempted disclosure.",
    "os.networkInterfaces() collects non-internal IPv4 addresses into localip, but localip is never transmitted. os.uptime() and its send call are commented out.",
    "The exported upload method generates random test data, JSON-serializes it, and writes it to a caller-configured HTTP request. It is not invoked by the install sidecar.",
    "No additional hidden payload, dynamic evaluation, credential-file read, persistence, or elevation is present. Hex is the only runtime encoding of collected values.",
    "JavaScriptCore execution with mocked OS modules and transport confirmed three GETs per version carrying synthetic username, hostname, and home directory; no real requests were made."
  ],
  "judgment_basis": "Silent install-time transmission of local identity to fixed third-party callback hosts is unrelated to measuring network speed. Authorized security-testing deployment and actual network success are unknown; neither is assumed.",
  "coverage_gap": "Existing two hostile findings describe the identity leak and its npm preinstall packaging, rather than two independent attack outcomes. No additional distinct hostile behavior is supported; no duplicate conviction was added.",
  "change": {
    "claim": "Requires Node HTTP/HTTPS module, including node:-prefixed forms; import alone proves no GET.",
    "from": "micro-behaviors/communications/http/get",
    "to": "metadata/import/builtin",
    "ids": [
      "node-prefixed-http-require",
      "node-prefixed-https-require",
      "node-http-module-required",
      "node-https-module-required"
    ],
    "preservation": "Matchers, type/platform scope, and notable criticality unchanged. The class-selector GET consumer references the relocated groups. No new directory or matcher was introduced.",
    "consumer_audit": "Only the class-selector GET composite names these IDs. Fourteen GET-directory consumers were inspected: they require requests, not imports, so retaining import-only membership would misstate their network leg. No ancestor selectors consume metadata/import or metadata/import/builtin.",
    "material_detection_losses": "None in the three supplied archives or the outside-batch ltidisafe 3.7.2, 3.7.3, 3.8.3 fixtures. Only import observations change IDs; actual GET and both hostile findings remain."
  },
  "validation_evidence": {
    "hex_identity_fixtures": "All nine existing flow/rename/logging/comment/disconnection controls passed.",
    "class_selector_fixtures": "All six existing GET-specific cases passed, including prefixed imports, wrong receiver, wrong URL, wrong method, non-HTTP, and comments.",
    "import_placement_fixtures": "check.py checks plain imports, node:-prefixed imports, and commented imports; real imports remain notable and no import-only case emits a GET trait.",
    "outside_batch": "All findings compared for ltidisafe 3.7.2, 3.7.3, and 3.8.3; no losses beyond the four-ID relocation map.",
    "unrelated_existing_failure": "The existing ltidisafe-review checker expects has-preinstall-script on noop-chain/package.json. This expectation fails both before and after this change; that fixture is unchanged."
  },
  "classifier_disagreement": "Before and after: every supplied archive has raw aggregate probability 0.9974145 but calibrated lvl=-1 and route cls=0 (unflagged). The hostile sidecar has raw probability 0.0065344968 and lvl=-1. Accurate hostile YAML findings persist; this is a retained classifier miss. The model emits a v18/v19 feature compatibility warning.",
